+
+### Demonstrated cause and correction
+
+Both original Server 2022 profiles reached all 351 registered tests: **349 passed,
+two failed** (`host_capabilities_portable`, `host_capabilities_portable_source`).
+Both passed `cli_install` and `cli_install_resources`. Independently retained
+Release and Debug diagnostics identify `kind=2`, Win32 `code=5`, `stage=4`
+(executable ancestors), before image open or `CreateProcessW`. Their rejected
+drive-root descriptors are identical:
+
+```text
+O:NSD:(A;OICI;FA;;;BA)(A;OICI;FA;;;SY)(A;OICIIO;GA;;;CO)(A;OICI;0x1200a9;;;BU)(A;CI;LC;;;BU)(A;CIIO;DC;;;BU)(A;;0x1200a9;;;WD)
+```
+
+The rejecting rule is **owner identity**, ahead of the ACE loop. `NS` denotes
+[Network Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/secauthz/sid-strings),
+which is outside this caller's existing trusted ancestor-owner set. The controlled
+native regression passes this exact in-memory descriptor to the production
+predicate and obtains access denied; changing **only** its owner to SYSTEM admits
+the identical ACE list. No real drive ownership or ACL is changed. The Runtime
+header factors descriptor evaluation out of the existing handle verifier so the
+test exercises the actual policy. It does not create a source capability from a
+descriptor or add a trusted SID.
+
+The Built-in Users entries do not cause this rejection. `0x1200a9` grants
+read/execute; directory `LC` has mask `0x4` (add subdirectory); `DC` has mask `0x2`
+(add file) and is inherit-only here. These masks must be interpreted as
+[file/directory access rights](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/file-access-rights-constants),
+not directory-service permission names. Inherit-only entries do not grant access
+to this parent; effective grants on an opened child are checked there. Creation
+of a new sibling alone does not authorize replacement of an existing checked
+child. Delete-child, deletion, DACL/owner modification, attribute/EA mutation and
+generic write/all grants to untrusted principals remain rejected. Network Service
+ownership cannot simply be admitted: owners normally have implicit DACL-modifying
+rights, subject to
+[OWNER RIGHTS semantics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/ad-ds/manage/understand-security-identifiers).
+This descriptor has no OWNER RIGHTS restriction that would establish a different
+trust contract.
+
+The permanent CI correction is **explicit test-caller staging**, using the existing
+native private-directory, file and SHA-256 providers. The harness approves its
+freshly built helper's exact digest, then the helper opens that regular source
+with no write/delete sharing, bounds its extent, creates an exclusive private
+directory and file under the trusted temp ancestry, copies with checked progress,
+checks source identity/extent/write time, flushes, applies private executable
+classification, and hashes the held destination again. The Python caller verifies
+the resulting file digest too. Digest mismatch and existing-root replacement
+attempts must fail at their expected checks. A failed candidate is never returned
+as an executable selection.
+
+Both existing native and source drivers pass this explicit private image to the
+unchanged process operation. The hosted diagnostics already demonstrate that the
+selected C: temp ancestry passes the original policy, while the D: build ancestry
+does not. Approval concerns the trusted harness's own build artifact; this is no
+authentication mechanism for arbitrary external images. There is no implicit
+copy/fallback in `process.start`, no weakening of ancestry checks and no runner
+security reconfiguration. Unix drivers retain their original executable path.
+
+Additional native regressions retain the original OWNER RIGHTS/private-leaf
+checks and test hostile image parents independently of hostile cwd parents,
+exact-descriptor owner/ACE discrimination, all existing mutation-mask classes,
+effective versus inherit-only grants, actual image/cwd junction rejection,
+standard-handle availability and observable stdout/stderr inheritance, exact exit
+status, repeated wait and cleanup. Junctions exist only under disposable fixture
+directories. Unicode, literal arguments and complete environments continue through
+the normal/O2 JIT and independently linked AOT source fixture.
